Fixed the seeded X5 defect at its root cause in:

- `firmware/libopencm3-examples/examples/stm32/f4/stm32f4-discovery/button/button.c`

### Root cause
`button_setup()` no longer enabled the GPIOA peripheral clock.  
Without `rcc_periph_clock_enable(RCC_GPIOA);`, reads from PA0 (user button) do not reflect button state, so the `if (gpio_get(GPIOA, GPIO0))` branch never affects timing.

### Fix applied
Restored the missing clock-enable call in `button_setup()`:

```c
rcc_periph_clock_enable(RCC_GPIOA);
```

This re-enables PA0 input sampling, so holding the on-board button now correctly changes the blink rate.
